WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.560
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.890
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.100
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.630
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.880
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.310
Go! Go!

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.690
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:43.960
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:50.960
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.340
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.780
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.910
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.390
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.750
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.120
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.520
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:21.430
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.200
If you like, could we have tea...

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.520
...together?

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.490
Yes! That's it! It's perfect!

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.190
Now, one more time, timed the way we just did it!

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:40.990
Together!

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.770
If you like, could we have tea...

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:46.990
...together?

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.750
What's with you two? Why so formal?

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.340
So, where do you want to go for tea?

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.760
Not you! Not YOU!

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.890
We're going to ask a beautiful lab assistant who passes by here every day at exactly 10:10 if...

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.150
...together...

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.260
...we could have some tea!

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.270
A beautiful lab assistant at 10:10?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.060
If you like, could we have tea...

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.440
...together?

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.450
Oh, Kazuya!

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.190
Hi, Kei. Used to your lab assistant job yet?

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.950
Oh, yes. Professor Yumi is a wonderful person.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:30.110
Oh, the beautiful lab assistant who passes by at 10:10 is you.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.130
What do you mean?

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.150
So, Kei! You're a friend of Kazuya's, huh?

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.630
We're also friends of his!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.500
If you like, could we have tea...

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.670
...together?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.640
Kazuya!

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.470
Kazuya! You forgot your report!

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.980
Together!

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.220
Hi, May. On an errand?

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.720
Yup! Here you go, Kazuya.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.280
Thanks. You're a lifesaver.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.770
You're welcome!

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.780
Anyway, I still have some cleaning to do, so I'd better go.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.150
May, hold on a second.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.850
Once I have Professor Yumi look at my report, I'll be all done.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.710
Let's go home together after that.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.400
In that case, I'd better get home fast.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.750
I have to get the cleaning done before you get home.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.650
If you'll excuse me—

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.170
Oh, May?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.080
I'm on my way home, too. Let's go together.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:20.860
Sure!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.800
Anyway, see you later.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.350
Maybe next time, we could have some tea...

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.170
...together!

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:30.190
Has to get it done before you get home, huh?! You're living...

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.280
...together!

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.800
In the same place?!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.340
So, what's with all these tasteless roses?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.250
A present for my beloved May, of course!

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.590
When she sees this, she'll fall into a mellow swoon!

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.770
As sweet as melon on a spoon!

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.500
The sweet, sweet melody of love! May! My love! So sweet!

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.170
She may be bigger now,

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.120
but she's still "that mini-Bot" from before!

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.860
In love, there are no boundaries, round trees, or foundries!

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.320
Be they robot or whatever, if I'm love with them, then I'm in love with them!

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.580
What's so great about that overgrown little kid?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.580
Her milkiness, silkiness, perfectness is what's so great!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.590
Love is great, oh, it is! Love!

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.100
Love. Big deal!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.420
Sara...

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.490
Why do I get all embarrassed when I think about that guy?!

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.110
May! Your soulmate, Kotaro Nanbara,

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:52.430
is coming to you with lavender roses!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:56.940
I'm sorry. Is this the way to Momijiyama City?

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.420
J-Just take the next exit...

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.360
Oh, I'm very close, aren't I? Thank you!

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:06.670
What was that?

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.200
No idea.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.610
Here.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.230
Miss, do you know where I can find "Kasumi House"?

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.200
<i>Mika... Mika...</i>

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:45.650
<i>Yamazaki...</i>

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.450
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.290
I'm home!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.310
Welcome home, Kazuya. I'll pour you a cold glass of milk.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.190
Please wait inside for me.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.790
<i>How long will the winds keep Mika and Yamazaki from their destiny?</i>

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.670
Hi, Kazuya!

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.960
Hello there.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.800
Hi there!

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.520
Hi, guys.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.630
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.170
May did this all herself.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.230
We used to do it together before.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.430
Kazuya, you have a guest.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.360
Kazuya dear! I've so wanted to meet you!

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.580
Hey, Kazuya! How long are you gonna hang onto her?!

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.120
I-I'm <i>not</i> hanging onto her!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.490
Unacceptable!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.370
Oh, my, my, my?

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.870
Please take those off.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.120
Oh, my, my, my!

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.970
So, Mami, you're saying my dad sent you to take care of me?

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.000
That's right! He did, Kazuya dear!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.240
You're dad's working overseas, isn't he?

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:00.310
Yeah, but he never said a thing about Mami.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.940
Wait, my sister at home might know.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.070
I'll call and ask.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.370
Oh, my, my, my?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.590
Oh, my, my, my...

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.700
Hi, Sis? Long time. It's Kazuya.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.090
Oh, Kaz! I haven't heard from you at all lately!

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.200
I was starting to get worried!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.130
Wow! Like a pro!

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.160
So beautifully compact. It's perfect!

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.600
Not a crease out of place!

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.220
Mami! You're much better than I am!

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.760
Not bad, Madam Mami.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.380
Oh, my, my, my...

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.260
Huh? Dad never sent me word about it.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.260
Mami, huh? Oh, wait!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:38.580
That's the same name as the cousin of that uncle in Kanazawa!

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.390
Well, you know Dad...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.100
Why are you putting that newspaper in water?

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.820
For this!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:54.400
When you use it to clean tatami mats and hardwood floors, they turn out bright and shiny!

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:58.480
Anyway, you should come home!
I haven't seen you for a year now!

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:02.430
I'll send you more of your favorite dish: somen!

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:10.600
We've had twenty-one somen-based meals,
including lunch boxes, in the past week alone!

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.010
I want to eat something else.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.010
But we still have so much left.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.880
Besides, I've already made them for lunch.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.380
Oh, my, my, my. Don't worry, May dear.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.980
Leave this to me.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.150
I just worry my little brother isn't eating enough.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.680
Is that big brother?

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.900
Yeah. Here, Midori wants to talk.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.010
Hello, big brother? Midori here!

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.790
Huh? Oh, I hear a girl there!

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.180
Do you finally have a girlfriend?

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:52.180
What happened with the landlady's daughter we met when you moved in?

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:52.870
Well?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.670
Th-They haven't heard about her, either!

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.760
My dad might've forgotten to contact us, though.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.270
Amazing!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.270
Mami made it all.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.500
Oh, my, my, my...

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.770
Come on, let's eat before it gets cold.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.230
"Eat while the iron's hot," as they say.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.740
Let's eat!

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:15.740
Delicious!

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.620
This really is great!

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.780
This is way better than anything I can make!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.600
Isn't this great, Kazuya?

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.490
We can have great food like this from now on!

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.210
Great! Great!

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.690
Exceptional at cooking and cleaning.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:35.220
In her cooking, the menu variety, taste, and nutritional balance are all perfect.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.390
Oh, my, my, my...

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.890
I'm still such an amateur! I'll try even harder!

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.830
So bright!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.860
Oh, my, my, my!

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.490
Oh, my, my, my. I'm home!

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.650
Oh, too late...

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.000
Here! Mt. Momiji milk!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.410
Thank you. I was just thinking I was thirsty.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.420
Oh, my, my, my. You're just like him.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.690
Huh? Like who?

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.380
Oh, my, my, my! Never mind!

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.880
Okay, then. I'll try my best!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.550
Even I can get the bathtub clean and shiny!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.590
Now to let the water out, and it's all clean!

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.100
H-H-Huh?

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:29.910
I-It's clogged!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.120
What's up, May?

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.830
Um, do you have anything for me to do?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.490
No, nothing special right now.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.880
Oh, I see...

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:12.370
What's wrong?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:17.110
U-Uh, nothing! I-I have some work to do outside!

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:25.440
May and Kazuya. Oh, my, my, my.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.630
Kazuya dear, do you have a moment?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.200
Sure. What's up?

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.630
I was wondering if you could run an errand for me.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:45.350
From the day I first laid eyes upon you,
my love has blossomed!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.850
You, in your plainness...

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.560
and I, in my finery!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.870
Here, to serve you...

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.190
the great Nanbara has arrived!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.810
Oh. Hi, Nanbara.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:12:01.610
May! As you have thrown my heart into disarray, I offer you these lavender roses!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.160
Here! Accept my love!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.450
Thank you...

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.050
Music!

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.000
Your smile is reward enough for me.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.700
Darling May, I want you to be my companion through life!

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.710
But, I can't cook or clean very well.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:23.180
Don't worry! That's all right!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.520
We can have our maid handle that!

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.450
What?! What's that supposed to mean?!

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.100
Oh? What's up, Nanbara?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.650
Kazuya, look at all the flowers Nanbara brought for me.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:39.710
Is this clear? These flowers are a present for May, not for you!

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.050
Right, right. Hi there, Sara.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.110
Um, uh, well...

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.770
H-Here! Take it!

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:48.700
Uh, thanks, Sara.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.680
Kazuya dear! May dear! Snack time!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:55.290
Oh?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.130
Oh, my, my, my? Guests?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:01.740
Oh, guests! Let's have all the guests we can!

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:07.180
Let's quest for guests and let them rest!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.190
Oh, my, my, my. Let's have a marriage meeting!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.360
I want all of you to use this opportunity to become friends.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.470
Go on, the time is now!

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:27.250
Mix! Mix!

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.610
This bodes well! Now begin!

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:33.120
<i>Marriage meeting, huh? Just what I wanted!</i>

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.620
<i>N-Now I can get Kazuya Saotome to myself.</i>

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.460
<i>A marriage meeting! Cool!</i>

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:42.460
<i>Shouldn't the number of men and women at a marriage meeting be balanced?</i>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.970
<i>This is a friendly gathering, right?</i>

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.470
<i>Marriage meeting. Ri-i-ight...</i>

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.730
Oh, my, my, my. Well, first comes question time, doesn't it?

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:53.270
Even the Buddha didn't know things the first three times.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.480
Anyone with a question, raise your hand!

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.480
Me! Me! ME!

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.860
Number one! I, Kotaro Nanbara, have a question for May!

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.890
Is there anyone in here that you really like?!

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.240
Naturally, it's me, Kotaro Nanbara, isn't it?

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.720
You've fallen for my irresistible charms, haven't you?!

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.930
You love the clear honesty in my eyes!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.090
My fashion sense is brilliant, isn't it?

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.420
The great Nanbara is wonderful, isn't he?!

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.900
Yes, that goes without saying!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.280
Oh, my, my, my. Anyone else have a question?

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.040
Um...

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:26.210
Yes? Sara dear?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.720
Wh-What are Kazuya's interests?

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.970
Um, let's see. Computers, basically.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.220
H-How about you?

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.440
R-Ramen...

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:36.240
And plenty of it!

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:39.000
Kazuya, do Ikariya and I make a good couple?

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:42.440
Not as good as May and I!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.190
Kazuya, what exactly is the difference between "like" and "love"—

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.490
None, as far as May confessing her feelings to me!

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.500
Kazuya, are you taking this fake marriage meeting seriously?

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.200
Fake or not, a marriage meeting is a marriage meeting!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.040
Am I any use to you, Kazuya?

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.580
I want you to be more useful to me than to Saotome!

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.230
Why's Nanbara answering everything?!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.460
Because the Earth revolves around me, that's why.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:08.530
Huh?

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.170
Oh, my, my, my, Kazuya dear. You're very popular, aren't you?

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.510
Um, well...

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.010
What am I doing here?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.720
Okay, talking time is over.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:21.730
Oh, my, my, my. Next up is confession time!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.360
Everyone, close your eyes. Close them tight!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:28.610
Okay, here we go. Everyone who likes Kazuya, raise your hands!

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:33.320
Ah, I see. I see.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:36.770
I see how you feel very clearly.

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:37.950
In that case...

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.960
Time to exchange nuptial cups!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:44.060
Go on, Kazuya! Drink up!

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.890
O-Oh, my! Look at all the tea stalks floating upright.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:51.220
What a lucky sign for you! And now to slice the cake!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.510
Oh, my, my, my!

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:56.350
Next is what you've waited for.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.010
The Love Machine bed.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.840
Love Machine?!

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:02.130
The meeting couple sleeps in it together.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.890
The Love Machine will ensure a far better relationship!

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.270
No way!

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.030
Oh, my, my, my...

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.790
The Love Machine is wonderfully appropriate!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.700
All hail the Love Machine! The Love Machine is the best!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.780
I LOVE THE LOVE MACHINE! YEAH!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:21.310
Come, May. Come on, to the Love Machine...

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:27.180
You want to do it, too, Ikariya?

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.040
Ikariya!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:35.870
Kazuya...

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:36.510
Yes?

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.750
I'm all ready for you.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:42.700
S-Sara...

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:44.550
Hurry up!

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.120
Y-Yes...

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.110
No, you don't!

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.380
Where do you think you're going, Kazuya?!

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:49.970
Kasumi!

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:53.150
A marriage meeting isn't peaceful. It's actually a war.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.030
Oh, my, my, my...

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.990
It's this late already?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:00.810
Okay! That's all for this time.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:03.040
May hasn't tried the Love Machine with me yet!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.000
She can't. We have to have dinner soon.

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:09.000
Oh, my, my, my. Come again!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.130
Aw, no way!

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:13.880
Oh, my, my, my. Everyone, help me.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.510
Rena dear, you peel the carrots. Kei dear, you make the dressing.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.220
Kasumi dear, you set the table. Okay, let's start!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.460
Right!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.740
Oh, my, my, my. May dear, will you do the shopping?

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.060
Okay! See you later!

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:31.770
See you later!

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:37.160
Oh, dear, dear, dear! I didn't give her my purse!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.240
Oh, my, my, my...

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:42.290
Kazuya dear, I'm sorry. Would you take this to May, please?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.200
Uh, sure.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.250
See you later!

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.210
Oh, my, my, my...

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.750
May!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:49.940
The purse! The purse!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.340
Here. You forgot this.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.660
Want to take a little rest?

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.670
It's been a while...

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:33.880
since we were alone like this.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.110
That's right.

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:38.980
Even though we've been together, we haven't had time to just relax and talk lately.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.930
I thought it was May!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.580
Play with us, May!

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.060
Masato! Miyuki!

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:48.390
C'mon, May! Kazuya! Play with us!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:49.740
Shall we?

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:50.540
Yeah!

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:52.900
Okay, let's go!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.070
All right, then!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.280
Here we go!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:59.320
This is great!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.160
We're home.

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.880
You're late! I'm really hungry!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.180
Sorry about that.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.560
We stopped to sit on the grass, and it ate up the time.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:26.240
It looks more like you ate up the grass.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:28.270
I want to eat some, too!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:30.790
We waited long enough for you guys...

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.350
Oh, Kazuya. Hold on.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.860
There you go.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:34.790
Then—

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.450
Oh, my, my, my! You're both filthy!

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:42.770
<i>Well, well, well.</i>

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:45.120
<i>Looks like it was a successful shopping trip.</i>

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.680
Here's the dinner you've been waiting for. Dig in!

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:52.830
Quite a variety, huh?

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.630
Oh, my, my, my. The TV should be off during dinner.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.130
Mami, you're a...

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.420
...cyber doll, right?

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:03.170
Didn't I mention that?

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.900
Still, we can see it now.

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.640
Oh, my, my, my. I didn't even think to mention it.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:12.770
Still, one more cyber doll here won't be any trouble, right, Kazuya dear?

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.490
Y-Yeah... As long as it's okay with Kasumi.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:17.150
Huh? Kasumi?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.720
Here we go. Here we go.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:49.760
I'll clear things up. You stay with Kazuya, May dear.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:51.970
You don't have that much time, you know.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.730
I don't have much time?

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.490
That's right. Because...

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:56.680
May!

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:59.770
The "Whirlwind of Love" special's starting soon!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.860
As I was saying.

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.540
There, there, there. Go and watch.

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:11.160
<i>Thanks to the sudden arrival of Mami, the expert housekeeper,</i>

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.910
<i>I'll have more time to be with Kazuya, and I'm glad!</i>

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:18.360
<i>Today, I got to slide on the grass,
and talk to him more than I have in a long time!</i>

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.450
<i>It was so much fun!</i>

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:23.300
<i>With all I can learn about cleaning and cooking from Mami,</i>

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.490
<i>I'll be able to do even more to take care of Kazuya!</i>

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:30.560
<i>All right, then! Tomorrow I'll do my best, too!</i>

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:46.700
When I'm with you, I blush till my ears turn red.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:51.230
I wonder why that is...

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:57.120
When I'm alone with you I can never seem to do anything right.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:05.270
I become so tongue-tied I can't speak at all.

00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:12.420
It's strange, don't you think? I think about it too much.

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:21.860
Is this love? I just can't accept that at all.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:28.400
I can't be honest. I want so much to be.

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:35.240
Someday, perhaps, you'll tell me

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:43.270
the true feelings that are in my heart.

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:47.720
Sara, here's a riddle for you. Here we go.

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.090
When you're thirsty, you're "kara-kara."

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:50.240
When a star shines, it's "kira-kira."

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:51.740
When you stand up too quickly, you're "kura-kura."

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:53.130
When you're excited, you're "hara-hara."

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:54.400
So, what does that make me?

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:55.260
"Ara-Ara!"

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:56.810
Wrong! The correct answer is "Mami"!

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:58.080
And you're happy with that?

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:00.350
"There's So Much I Want!"
